    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **salutation** feature on the `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow, following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions in the repo.\n\n**What \"salutation\" does:** the create request may include an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner then exposes a derived, read-only `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title was supplied.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (the DTOs are generated from this at build time):\n   - Added `title` (optional string) to the `OwnerFields` input schema.\n   - Added `salutation` (read-only string) to the `Owner` output schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so it persists and round-trips.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(salutation(owner))\")` plus a `salutation(Owner)` default method implementing the compose/fallback rule. `title` maps automatically by name in both directions (input DTO\u2192entity, entity\u2192output DTO).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialect scripts (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column was required for the value to persist; I updated the others for consistency.\n\nThe new `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes.",
